(6540177, 972567, 30861, '<td valign="top">Pedantic observation: "wherefore" means "why", or "for what reason" -- Juliet is asking, basically, "Why the HELL did you have to be a Montague, Romeo?"<br/> <br/><i>JULIET:<br/>O Romeo, Romeo! wherefore art thou Romeo?<br/>Deny thy father and refuse thy name;<br/>Or, if thou wilt not, be but sworn my love,<br/>And I''ll no longer be a Capulet.</i> <br/> <br/>She''s actually offering to abandon her own family to be with him; the Montagues and Capulets are bitter enemies, have been for generations.<br/> <br/>Cool shot, though :-)</td>', 'Pedantic observation: "wherefore" means "why", or "for what reason" -- Juliet is asking, basically, "Why the HELL did you have to be a Montague, Romeo?" JULIET:O Romeo, Romeo! wherefore art thou Romeo?Deny thy father and refuse thy name;Or, if thou wilt not, be but sworn my love,And I''ll no longer be a Capulet.  She''s actually offering to abandon her own family to be with him; the Montagues and Capulets are bitter enemies, have been for generations. Cool shot, though :-)', '2011-09-14 19:39:16.000000', NULL, 1),
