(6549904, 973140, 61084, '<td valign="top">Congrats Oliver. I enjoyed this photo very much. Nice choice regarding the B&amp;W conversion. I think color would have lessened the visual impact.</td>', 'Congrats Oliver. I enjoyed this photo very much. Nice choice regarding the B&W conversion. I think color would have lessened the visual impact.', '2011-09-24 13:22:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6550531, 973226, 16106, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by herfotoman:</b></div><hr/><i> Such elegant lighting. How big is the lightbox? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=975330" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16106/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_975330.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16106/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_975330.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/16106/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_975330.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>This big. Taken about 30 seconds before the Waldo shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by herfotoman: Such elegant lighting. How big is the lightbox?     This big. Taken about 30 seconds before the Waldo shot.', '2011-09-25 16:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6551920, 973360, 123837, '<td valign="top">This is an incredible photo! Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'This is an incredible photo! Congrats on the ribbon!', '2011-09-26 18:04:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6552602, 972747, 10686, '<td valign="top">From the <b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, this is well done and I think the score and ranking reflect that. It certainly meets the challenge and from a technical standpoint, the B&amp;W looks great. I think you made the right choice with B&amp;W. The composition, using the near mountains, the far mountains and the sky to divide the image into thirds is excellent. <br/> <br/>I''m going to make a few suggestions and technical comments on some other possibilities to consider.<br/> <br/>First, the paraglider. I didn''t know what it was until I read the comments. I thought the canopy was a bird. I''d like to have seen it directly from the front or back and then it would have been more identifiable. Unless you''re working with the pilot, there''s not much you could have done though aside from hope.<br/> <br/>Second, the foreground. The closest thing to the viewer in the image is the mountains at the bottom, which are still pretty far away. It makes me feel like I''m flying. It would be nice to try some closer foreground in the bottom of the shot. You might have to lay down on the ground...<br/> <br/>Overall though this is a solid image and I just want to give you some things to consider for the future or in processing another shot you might have made on this same trip.<br/> <br/>Spork</td>', 'From the Critique Club  First of all, this is well done and I think the score and ranking reflect that. It certainly meets the challenge and from a technical standpoint, the B&W looks great. I think you made the right choice with B&W. The composition, using the near mountains, the far mountains and the sky to divide the image into thirds is excellent.  I''m going to make a few suggestions and technical comments on some other possibilities to consider. First, the paraglider. I didn''t know what it was until I read the comments. I thought the canopy was a bird. I''d like to have seen it directly from the front or back and then it would have been more identifiable. Unless you''re working with the pilot, there''s not much you could have done though aside from hope. Second, the foreground. The closest thing to the viewer in the image is the mountains at the bottom, which are still pretty far away. It makes me feel like I''m flying. It would be nice to try some closer foreground in the bottom of the shot. You might have to lay down on the ground... Overall though this is a solid image and I just want to give you some things to consider for the future or in processing another shot you might have made on this same trip. Spork', '2011-09-27 13:47:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6556350, 972878, 29011, '<td valign="top">It''s a fine a shot. Just, no love for cats on DPC :P<br/></td>', 'It''s a fine a shot. Just, no love for cats on DPC :P', '2011-10-01 00:55:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6564900, 972878, 124815, '<td valign="top">i]makes a lot of sense in its own and good fulfillment of the challenge[/i]<br/>I repeat my first comment during the voting mostly because it seems to be a rare quality here. A lot of people meet the challenge but produce inconsequential images. Pictures that outside the challenge are meaningless. <br/> <br/>This picture has a meaning and its own beauty and  Waldo does not need to be searched using a magnifying lens.<br/></td>', 'i]makes a lot of sense in its own and good fulfillment of the challenge[/i]I repeat my first comment during the voting mostly because it seems to be a rare quality here. A lot of people meet the challenge but produce inconsequential images. Pictures that outside the challenge are meaningless.  This picture has a meaning and its own beauty and  Waldo does not need to be searched using a magnifying lens.', '2011-10-09 23:23:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6612790, 972904, 12611, '<td valign="top">beautiful and great contrast.</td>', 'beautiful and great contrast.', '2011-12-07 11:07:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6626112, 973326, 64446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by snaffles:</b></div><hr/><i> Hmm, Waldo may be that slightly blodgy/human body form atop the first light coloured mezzanine. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hi Susan - no, he''s in the 2nd gap on the left side... actually you can only see his hand...<br/>Thanks for looking and commenting.<br/>G</td>', 'Originally posted by snaffles: Hmm, Waldo may be that slightly blodgy/human body form atop the first light coloured mezzanine.  Hi Susan - no, he''s in the 2nd gap on the left side... actually you can only see his hand...Thanks for looking and commenting.G', '2011-12-26 23:06:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6781970, 973339, 137320, '<td valign="top">I updated the description after all this time so people can understand a little better how this shot was done. P.S. my wife has gotten over the fact that she was told she wasn''t human several times in the comments! lol</td>', 'I updated the description after all this time so people can understand a little better how this shot was done. P.S. my wife has gotten over the fact that she was told she wasn''t human several times in the comments! lol', '2012-05-30 20:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6911539, 972048, 152252, '<td valign="top">Great image. High contrast and triangles make it very interesting. And Waldo''s quiet, almost unnoticeable presence of course :) Even more impressive that it was basic editing. Congrats!</td>', 'Great image. High contrast and triangles make it very interesting. And Waldo''s quiet, almost unnoticeable presence of course :) Even more impressive that it was basic editing. Congrats!', '2012-11-22 19:44:35.000000', NULL, 0);
